# Files that MUST keep Unix line endings regardless of which machine checks them out.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and runs on a Mac. A shell
# script checked out with CRLF fails there with `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env
# bash^M`, which is an obscure way to discover that the nightly backup has never
# once run. launchd is equally unforgiving about a plist with CRLF.
#
# Deliberately narrow: a blanket `* text=auto eol=lf` would renormalise every file
# in the repo in a single unreviewable commit.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.plist text eol=lf
